WEBVTT

00:08.425 --> 00:13.680
[male voice] I am of the genie,
a spirit created from a smokeless fire.

00:14.431 --> 00:19.102
We were created on Thursday,
the day after the angels were made.

00:23.690 --> 00:25.358
[magical music playing]

00:27.986 --> 00:31.030
If you can hear me
speaking in your language,

00:31.114 --> 00:32.490
that is because

00:33.074 --> 00:35.118
I am a genie.

00:35.201 --> 00:36.911
[alarm chiming]

00:39.956 --> 00:41.499
Genie, shut off the alarm.

00:42.959 --> 00:46.087
[male Genie] With our supernatural
strength and magical powers,

00:46.171 --> 00:47.839
we genies grew arrogant.

00:49.048 --> 00:51.843
We aspired to become
the greatest of all beings.

00:52.761 --> 00:54.387
But I had no interest in that.

00:55.388 --> 00:57.515
Becoming greater than him.

00:57.599 --> 01:00.310
[scoffs] That would be such a hassle.

01:04.105 --> 01:06.191
Even so, the angels were sent down

01:06.274 --> 01:08.985
with orders to decimate the haughty Genie.

01:09.986 --> 01:13.823
After 300 long years,
the war finally ended.

01:15.492 --> 01:18.620
And so did the lives of all genies,
save a few,

01:18.703 --> 01:20.038
including my own.

01:21.664 --> 01:24.167
I took refuge in a lamp.

01:25.877 --> 01:27.545
Once the world was purified,

01:27.629 --> 01:29.798
the very next day, Friday,

01:29.881 --> 01:32.467
he created a new species to replace us.

01:33.218 --> 01:38.097
None other than you, humans,
molded out of clay.

01:39.933 --> 01:43.603
And then,
he presented to us his first human,

01:43.686 --> 01:45.563
and commanded us to bow our heads.

01:46.189 --> 01:49.734
All the angels and surviving genies
bowed before his creation,

01:50.318 --> 01:53.071
but I refused.

01:53.154 --> 01:54.030
[water trickles]

01:58.201 --> 01:59.244
[gulps]

01:59.327 --> 02:00.495
-[cup thuds]
-Ah.

02:01.871 --> 02:02.705
APRIL 5TH
FLYING OUT

02:02.789 --> 02:05.834
I, created from ancient fire,

02:06.835 --> 02:08.670
refused to bow my head

02:09.337 --> 02:10.880
to a mortal built from clay.

02:11.673 --> 02:14.801
Enraged, he threw me from heaven.

02:15.426 --> 02:16.636
[thunder rumbling]

02:16.719 --> 02:20.306
I fell downwards to hell
and made just one request.

02:21.975 --> 02:23.601
I would accept my fate

02:24.185 --> 02:27.564
on the condition that I'd be given
the task of corrupting humans

02:28.606 --> 02:30.692
and landing them in hell.

02:33.027 --> 02:38.700
I swore to show him once and for all
how pathetic his beloved mortals were.

02:38.783 --> 02:41.161
He granted my request.

02:41.744 --> 02:43.746
Yet, there was a catch.

02:43.830 --> 02:45.081
[whimpers]

02:47.167 --> 02:48.626
-You got all that?
-[barking]

02:49.544 --> 02:52.172
[AI Genie] He said,
"I shall approve your request."

02:52.255 --> 02:53.923
"But if you happen to meet

02:54.007 --> 02:56.676
[over speaker] even one pure human soul,

02:56.759 --> 02:59.387
you will fall to even greater depths
of isolation and despair…"

02:59.470 --> 03:03.016
-Why is it rambling like that? What now?
-[distorted] …than hell itself.

03:03.641 --> 03:07.145
[male Genie] Thus, the legend
of the three wishes was born.

03:07.228 --> 03:09.647
That famous story you humans all know of.

03:10.356 --> 03:15.445
I left hell, inhabiting vessels
like lamps, rings, and jars.

03:19.115 --> 03:23.536
Those who summoned me
were granted three wishes.

03:24.370 --> 03:26.998
Humans are lazy, selfish, arrogant.

03:27.081 --> 03:30.835
Never satisfied with their lot
and eager to betray each other.

03:30.919 --> 03:34.464
And so they corrupted themselves,
while I was vindicated.

03:35.340 --> 03:38.343
I saw the fall of mortals.

03:39.218 --> 03:40.637
But you…

03:40.720 --> 03:43.348
you, from that small land in the East,

03:43.431 --> 03:45.266
even as you drew your final breaths,

03:45.350 --> 03:47.644
you spent your three wishes on others.

03:47.727 --> 03:49.938
[scoffs] This cannot stand.

03:50.021 --> 03:53.775
You little girl.
Little girl molded from clay.

03:53.858 --> 03:55.902
You small, dying human.

03:57.153 --> 03:59.113
I shall observe your death.

04:00.156 --> 04:02.450
I shall take up a handful of dirt,

04:02.533 --> 04:04.786
dirt made from your flesh and bones.

04:05.495 --> 04:07.455
My lamp may be buried even deeper

04:07.538 --> 04:10.166
than the depths of darkness
because of you.

04:10.250 --> 04:13.962
But even so, I will not bow my head
to one so lowly as you,

04:14.045 --> 04:15.755
who was molded from clay.

04:15.838 --> 04:18.174
I shall remember your gaze.

04:18.758 --> 04:20.969
I shall remember the smell of your clay.

04:21.803 --> 04:23.888
If a new master should summon me

04:23.972 --> 04:27.892
so that I am able to be
of this world again, then…

04:28.810 --> 04:32.605
I will search every corner
until I find your soul.

04:33.439 --> 04:35.942
I shall do whatever it takes
to corrupt you,

04:36.693 --> 04:37.986
and kill you.

04:38.611 --> 04:39.821
Remember this,

04:40.488 --> 04:42.031
for I will seek you out.

04:42.115 --> 04:44.409
-[wind gusting]
-My name…

04:47.036 --> 04:48.496
is Iblis.

04:51.582 --> 04:53.584
[theme music playing]

05:48.848 --> 05:51.559
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

05:54.854 --> 05:56.272
Gogung set. Thank you.

05:56.355 --> 05:57.523
Just a few minutes.

06:10.953 --> 06:13.706
[sighs] I need you to stop.
Stop doing this.

06:13.790 --> 06:15.458
Every year, you come here.

06:15.541 --> 06:16.793
You think I didn't notice?

06:17.418 --> 06:20.630
The same table on the same day,
every year for ten years.

06:21.422 --> 06:22.882
Enough already.

06:22.965 --> 06:24.383
I've been aware of you.

06:24.467 --> 06:25.718
Of course you're aware.

06:26.594 --> 06:30.014
After all, those bags of cash dropped off
by my aunt these last ten years

06:30.098 --> 06:32.141
have given her the chance
to take pictures of me.

06:33.684 --> 06:34.602
Right, Mother?

06:35.228 --> 06:36.229
[sighs]

06:40.316 --> 06:42.735
My sister says not to worry about money.

06:42.819 --> 06:45.071
-Just look after of Ka-young.
-Look after her?

06:45.696 --> 06:47.115
Am I to be her mother now?
Is that it?

06:47.198 --> 06:49.200
Just make sure
she doesn't look for her real mother.

06:49.283 --> 06:51.744
-For God's sake! That wretched bitch!
-[gasps]

06:52.328 --> 06:54.205
So her mother's dead. Is that it?

06:54.288 --> 06:55.998
What person does that?

06:56.707 --> 06:58.876
Good God! She's a little girl.

07:00.128 --> 07:03.422
She just abandoned her baby girl
for being difficult!

07:08.678 --> 07:10.680
[crying]

07:10.763 --> 07:13.099
[sentimental music playing]

07:18.104 --> 07:20.148
[continues crying]

07:31.033 --> 07:33.786
[Ka-young] That's when
Grandma started her chili garden.

07:33.870 --> 07:36.289
Each year, it grew more and more,
her chilies taking over…

07:36.372 --> 07:37.623
Just stop this.

07:38.458 --> 07:39.542
Say what you mean.

07:39.625 --> 07:42.253
-Don't be so mysterious about it.
-Stop interrupting.

07:43.379 --> 07:46.591
Your youngest daughter is speaking to you
for the first time in 20 years.

07:46.674 --> 07:48.217
[cell phone vibrating]

07:56.142 --> 07:57.101
Chilies.

07:57.185 --> 08:00.271
Grew, and grew, and grew unmanageable.

08:01.063 --> 08:01.939
Swarming.

08:02.023 --> 08:05.109
[voice shaking] How? How did you find us?

08:06.402 --> 08:07.528
Are you kidding?

08:08.821 --> 08:10.072
You must be glad to get your ID.

08:11.574 --> 08:12.533
Yeah, thrilled.

08:12.617 --> 08:15.495
RESIDENT REGISTRATION
CERTIFIED COPIES, EXTRACTIONS

08:16.120 --> 08:17.830
One copy of my residence record, please.

08:18.831 --> 08:20.833
[suspenseful music plays]

08:22.710 --> 08:24.003
You're Ka-young.

08:25.963 --> 08:27.381
Why are you here?

08:27.465 --> 08:28.966
I did some research.

08:29.050 --> 08:32.595
My mother bought this building
and gave it to you to manage for her.

08:33.304 --> 08:34.388
Where have they gone?

08:35.056 --> 08:38.351
My whole family,
seeing as they're not dead?

08:42.355 --> 08:44.357
[bright music plays]

08:49.403 --> 08:50.571
Gogung set. Thank you.

08:51.989 --> 08:53.282
Gogung set. Thank you.

08:54.450 --> 08:55.368
Gogung set. Thank you.

08:56.744 --> 08:57.912
Gogung set. Thank you.

09:03.292 --> 09:06.879
What awful things do you do
for your hand to-- [sighs]

09:06.963 --> 09:09.757
You know as well as I do why I left you.

09:09.840 --> 09:11.342
I see the money I sent wasn't wasted.

09:11.425 --> 09:15.471
I paid for that. Full price too.
Earned entirely on my own.

09:16.055 --> 09:18.849
Your contributions
were all given to charity.

09:21.060 --> 09:22.186
These hands?

09:23.479 --> 09:27.316
You must not have bothered
to even ask my aunt what I do for work.

09:28.734 --> 09:31.320
My work involves cuts, scratches, burns.

09:31.404 --> 09:32.405
Now you're wondering

09:33.239 --> 09:35.157
if you have a murderer for a daughter.

09:35.241 --> 09:36.284
[breathes shakily]

09:39.453 --> 09:41.747
Grandma said we must
always choose kindness.

09:44.250 --> 09:45.668
I know that look.

09:48.629 --> 09:49.880
You're so afraid.

09:49.964 --> 09:51.632
[tense music plays]

09:53.634 --> 09:55.678
You say you learned how to be kind?

09:55.761 --> 09:57.722
How about fear? Do you feel that?

09:57.805 --> 09:59.849
You know I abandoned you
because you can't.

09:59.932 --> 10:02.393
You never even bothered
to try to teach me!

10:02.476 --> 10:04.562
-[dishes clanking]
-[sighs]

10:04.645 --> 10:05.938
[patrons murmuring]

10:06.606 --> 10:08.274
[woman] The thing is, ma'am,

10:09.609 --> 10:12.320
someone like Ka-young
cannot be taught these things.

10:12.403 --> 10:13.654
But why?

10:14.530 --> 10:16.157
We have a duty to try, don't we?

10:16.240 --> 10:18.492
I don't care what everyone says.

10:18.576 --> 10:19.952
I must help her somehow.

10:20.620 --> 10:22.705
Please, at least tell me about the class.

10:22.788 --> 10:25.708
What did Ka-young do
during with the frog dissection?

10:25.791 --> 10:27.752
Did she not do it properly?

10:27.835 --> 10:29.795
No. She actually did it perfectly.

10:30.921 --> 10:34.592
Forgive me… why am I here, then?

10:34.675 --> 10:37.678
That class was over
two months ago, in April.

10:37.762 --> 10:40.556
All Ka-young wants to do is dissect frogs.

10:40.640 --> 10:42.975
She's begged me every single day since.

10:43.809 --> 10:46.604
She asks all the time
why we don't do it more.

10:46.687 --> 10:48.689
It's all she wants to do now.

10:55.863 --> 10:56.906
[chuckles]

10:58.157 --> 10:59.116
[knife clinks]

11:02.453 --> 11:03.454
[shrieks]

11:03.537 --> 11:05.456
Grandma! Grandma, that hurts!

11:05.539 --> 11:07.583
-The frog is in pain too.
-[whimpers]

11:07.667 --> 11:10.127
The frog can't even tell you
how much it hurts!

11:10.211 --> 11:11.629
Damn you!

11:12.672 --> 11:15.257
[young Ka-young gasping and whimpering]

11:16.967 --> 11:18.803
[suffocates]
I can't breathe! Let go!

11:18.886 --> 11:21.055
-[wheezing]
-Grandma can't breathe either.

11:21.138 --> 11:23.265
[grunting] Let me go!

11:23.349 --> 11:25.935
I'll kill you, Grandma!
I'm gonna kill you!

11:26.018 --> 11:27.728
-[wheezing]
-Let me go, okay?

11:27.812 --> 11:29.855
If you let me go, I'll let you go.

11:29.939 --> 11:30.898
[grunting]

11:30.981 --> 11:32.233
[bones crunching softly]

11:32.316 --> 11:33.859
[grunts and gasps]

11:33.943 --> 11:35.945
[sentimental music plays]

11:37.571 --> 11:40.699
[grunting]

11:45.204 --> 11:46.831
Grandma, that hurts!

11:46.914 --> 11:49.041
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

11:49.125 --> 11:51.460
[gasping heavily]

11:51.544 --> 11:55.172
If you hug someone, I will hug you too.

11:55.756 --> 11:56.590
[whimpers]

11:56.674 --> 12:00.010
But if you cut someone,
then I will cut you too.

12:00.094 --> 12:00.928
[whimpers]

12:01.011 --> 12:02.638
And if you kill someone,

12:04.223 --> 12:05.808
I will kill you too.

12:07.268 --> 12:10.062
These are our rules, Ka-young. Got it?

12:10.146 --> 12:13.357
[whimpers] It hurts! Let me go!

12:13.441 --> 12:15.109
Remember the pain.

12:15.192 --> 12:17.111
The pain will help you learn.

12:18.237 --> 12:19.822
You must memorize it.

12:19.905 --> 12:21.115
[cries]

12:21.198 --> 12:22.199
Ka-young.

12:23.200 --> 12:25.453
Memorize my face, okay?

12:25.536 --> 12:26.620
This is sorrow.

12:27.371 --> 12:28.747
When I'm like this,

12:29.957 --> 12:32.793
when I have this look, it means that

12:32.877 --> 12:33.961
you'll die,

12:34.753 --> 12:37.047
and I die along with you. Understand?

12:37.131 --> 12:38.883
[crying]

12:41.177 --> 12:42.511
[sobs]

12:43.512 --> 12:44.722
I forgot it!

12:46.015 --> 12:48.809
I forgot the face! Do it again!

12:49.768 --> 12:51.437
[continues sobbing]

12:51.520 --> 12:53.606
[both sobbing]

12:53.689 --> 12:55.983
[sentimental music continues]

13:13.417 --> 13:15.211
[sobbing continues]

13:20.925 --> 13:21.926
[sniffles]

13:24.094 --> 13:26.096
I'm better now. I'm not sad.

13:26.805 --> 13:28.807
This face is hopeful.

13:29.475 --> 13:31.018
A hopeful face.

13:32.770 --> 13:34.563
[laughing]

13:36.357 --> 13:38.067
[Ka-young] So after that,

13:38.150 --> 13:40.861
I never hurt anything. I had rules.

13:41.695 --> 13:42.821
But, you know,

13:43.906 --> 13:45.950
life after that stopped being fun.

13:46.659 --> 13:47.660
I'm so bored, Mom.

13:47.743 --> 13:49.119
So what are you saying--

13:49.203 --> 13:50.704
Don't interrupt me. Got it?

13:51.372 --> 13:52.373
[breathes shakily]

13:53.624 --> 13:54.667
I dramas, they cry.

13:54.750 --> 13:57.628
Those soap operas,
they just sob their eyes out.

13:58.379 --> 14:00.839
I've always wondered, would Mom cry?

14:00.923 --> 14:03.509
I suppose I was… curious.

14:05.135 --> 14:06.887
Alas, neither of us is crying.

14:08.055 --> 14:10.307
Grandma sometimes cries in secret.

14:10.391 --> 14:12.059
I assume that…

14:12.142 --> 14:13.185
it's because of me.

14:13.269 --> 14:14.228
[breath shudders]

14:14.311 --> 14:15.312
It would make sense.

14:15.396 --> 14:18.774
But if Grandma ever cries again
because of you…

14:20.734 --> 14:23.445
then I will wrap my hands
around your neck.

14:24.822 --> 14:27.783
Until you can't make
any expression at all.

14:27.867 --> 14:28.701
Until the end.

14:28.784 --> 14:30.703
[tense music plays]

14:33.497 --> 14:35.916
I came to tell you this
in case you finally talk to me.

14:36.000 --> 14:37.501
Now that you have…

14:39.461 --> 14:40.462
I won't return.

14:43.966 --> 14:45.009
Farewell, Mom.

14:52.766 --> 14:54.768
[watch ticking]

15:14.121 --> 15:15.956
[breathes heavily]

15:28.135 --> 15:29.637
[cell phone vibrates]

15:29.720 --> 15:32.222
THIS IS DUBI-DUBAI TOURS
PLEASE BRING AN EXTRA LAYER

15:39.438 --> 15:40.439
[camel snorts]

15:40.522 --> 15:41.398
[both] Yeah!

15:42.441 --> 15:46.862
-[laughter]
-[woman] Oh, my goodness! It's so amazing!

15:46.946 --> 15:48.030
Say "Dubai!"

15:48.113 --> 15:49.365
Dubai!

15:51.492 --> 15:52.993
[imitates in dull tone] Dubai!

15:53.077 --> 15:54.995
[woman] Dubai!

15:55.079 --> 15:56.372
[woman chuckles]

15:56.455 --> 15:58.540
Do you see that dust cloud there?

15:58.624 --> 15:59.792
In Arabic culture,

15:59.875 --> 16:04.213
they refer to that phenomenon
as the "waltzing genie."

16:04.296 --> 16:05.923
-[woman gasps]
-[girl] No way. The Genie?

16:06.006 --> 16:07.633
You mean like a lamp genie? [gasps]

16:08.217 --> 16:09.093
Wow, incredible!

16:09.176 --> 16:11.929
[guide] All right, everyone.
It looks like a sandstorm could form soon.

16:12.012 --> 16:13.847
Are you all set to continue onwards?

16:13.931 --> 16:15.849
[laughs] You forgot we're Korean!

16:15.933 --> 16:19.019
Right, masks on, everyone. Let's go!

16:19.603 --> 16:21.313
[guide] We still have about an hour,

16:21.397 --> 16:23.399
-so feel free to keep taking photos.
-Whoo-hoo!

16:23.482 --> 16:25.317
-[tourists] Okay.
-A waltz is a duo.

16:25.401 --> 16:28.195
That cloud is all alone. Ridiculous.

16:28.278 --> 16:30.322
Oh, you're right. That's really strange.

16:31.031 --> 16:32.282
Wow, you're right!

16:32.908 --> 16:35.661
My goodness, dear. You're hilarious!

16:35.744 --> 16:36.704
[laughing]

16:36.787 --> 16:38.664
Gosh. Honestly. So--

16:38.747 --> 16:40.416
Which resort are you staying at?

16:41.709 --> 16:43.502
Whoa! Look at the genie! [exclaims]

16:43.585 --> 16:45.504
[girl] Mom. Mom, wait for me.

16:46.130 --> 16:48.632
[woman] Waltz! Waltz!

16:48.716 --> 16:50.384
[wind rumbling]

17:06.900 --> 17:07.985
[cell phone vibrates]

17:09.987 --> 17:11.321
[Min-ji] How's the desert?

17:11.405 --> 17:15.534
CHOI MIN-JI

17:15.617 --> 17:18.370
[Ka-young] Vast, hot, and windy.

17:19.038 --> 17:21.290
Perfect for burying a family of four.

17:21.373 --> 17:23.792
[Min-ji] Stop that!
Ticktock, ticktock, ticktock

17:27.796 --> 17:30.257
-[exhales deeply]
-[watch ticking]

17:33.552 --> 17:35.012
-[boot thuds]
-[gasps]

17:35.888 --> 17:37.681
[grunts]

17:39.266 --> 17:41.351
[mysterious music plays]

17:55.365 --> 17:57.284
[shouting] Why are you in my way?

17:57.367 --> 17:58.410
[lamp thuds]

17:59.328 --> 18:00.954
You abandoned your daughter.

18:01.580 --> 18:02.456
[lamp thuds]

18:02.539 --> 18:05.459
What pain did I cause you?
Your damn face of fear!

18:05.542 --> 18:09.129
You didn't even pretend.
Rubbing your amazing skin in my face!

18:09.213 --> 18:11.298
Your life was so…

18:11.381 --> 18:13.133
[grunts, pants]

18:13.217 --> 18:14.218
easy.

18:15.594 --> 18:17.846
That Gogung meal isn't even good.

18:17.930 --> 18:19.973
And you overcharge!

18:20.057 --> 18:20.891
[lamp thuds]

18:20.974 --> 18:22.893
[panting]

18:34.321 --> 18:36.365
[gasps] Huh?

18:37.825 --> 18:39.701
How'd that lamp get back here?

18:43.163 --> 18:44.164
Who did that?

18:44.748 --> 18:46.625
Show yourself, you coward!

18:47.501 --> 18:49.419
[wind rumbling]

18:49.503 --> 18:51.588
[breathing heavily]

18:57.177 --> 18:58.137
Hmm.

18:59.555 --> 19:00.556
[rattling]

19:00.639 --> 19:02.558
[muffled male voice] Whoa!
Why are we shaking?

19:02.641 --> 19:03.475
[rattling]

19:03.559 --> 19:04.726
What's going on?

19:05.435 --> 19:06.937
What's all this noise?

19:07.020 --> 19:08.605
-[rattling]
-[groans loudly]

19:08.689 --> 19:10.149
Ejllael! Stop that!

19:10.232 --> 19:12.317
[wind blowing]

19:14.486 --> 19:17.156
[captivating music plays]

19:20.325 --> 19:21.702
[wind gusting]

19:23.328 --> 19:26.456
[woman] Whoa!
Now that's what I call the waltz!

19:26.540 --> 19:27.666
[woman laughs excitedly]

19:27.749 --> 19:30.210
[girl] Wow, amazing. It's incredible!

19:30.294 --> 19:32.296
[wind continues gusting]

19:44.933 --> 19:47.102
[captivating music continues]

20:05.495 --> 20:06.496
[Iblis scoffs]

20:09.791 --> 20:11.835
One move and I kill you.

20:12.961 --> 20:13.962
[scoffs softly]

20:16.840 --> 20:17.966
Your hair…

20:19.718 --> 20:21.678
Who are you? You followed me?

20:25.057 --> 20:26.433
[sniffing]

20:29.978 --> 20:31.230
I said don't move.

20:33.857 --> 20:34.858
That smell,

20:35.609 --> 20:37.152
it's the clay.

20:37.236 --> 20:38.278
The same one.

20:38.904 --> 20:40.072
It's you…

20:41.156 --> 20:42.783
all those years ago.

20:43.700 --> 20:44.660
[chuckles softly]

20:45.327 --> 20:47.120
It's been almost a millennium.

20:48.288 --> 20:49.414
[grunts]

20:49.498 --> 20:51.541
Yikes, I almost got stabbed. [grunting]

20:54.211 --> 20:55.796
[panting]

20:59.883 --> 21:01.134
Huh?

21:01.218 --> 21:03.011
[Ka-young] Who is this moron?

21:03.095 --> 21:05.847
WHO IS THIS MORON?
[Iblis] "Who is this moron?"

21:07.224 --> 21:10.602
I am an ancient spirit. Older than time.

21:10.686 --> 21:11.770
[Iblis clears throat]

21:12.396 --> 21:13.897
All right. Listen, young girl.

21:14.481 --> 21:16.566
My name… [grunts]

21:16.650 --> 21:17.943
is Iblis.

21:18.026 --> 21:20.737
I was created from smokeless… [gags]

21:21.446 --> 21:23.532
Did you have to shake the lamp that hard?

21:23.615 --> 21:24.700
[sniffs]

21:24.783 --> 21:25.742
[clears throat]

21:27.995 --> 21:29.955
People know me as… [gags]

21:30.038 --> 21:31.456
as…

21:31.540 --> 21:32.791
[retching]

21:33.959 --> 21:35.669
You shook it too much.

21:35.752 --> 21:37.587
[retching]

21:38.672 --> 21:39.965
Hey, wait.

21:40.924 --> 21:42.342
My lamp.

21:42.426 --> 21:44.469
I told you to wait. I know you're her.

21:44.553 --> 21:45.846
[grunts]

21:45.929 --> 21:47.806
I am the Genie!

21:47.889 --> 21:49.433
[Iblis pants]

21:49.516 --> 21:52.144
The spirit of the lamp,
the Genie, you know!

21:58.942 --> 22:00.944
[mysterious music plays]

22:04.865 --> 22:08.910
This is its real length, but I usually
wear it nice and short like earlier.

22:10.996 --> 22:12.247
[chuckles softly]

22:12.331 --> 22:13.498
Okay.

22:15.500 --> 22:16.501
This is…

22:17.252 --> 22:18.337
unexpected.

22:18.420 --> 22:19.671
How'd you get in here?

22:19.755 --> 22:22.215
Well, I did say quite loudly earlier.

22:22.299 --> 22:24.134
I am the Genie of the lamp.

22:28.805 --> 22:32.184
I can go anywhere I desire, "Ki Ka-young."

22:33.435 --> 22:35.562
You speak my language
but you butcher my name?

22:35.645 --> 22:37.189
[laughing]

22:37.272 --> 22:39.441
It appears you don't yet grasp
what's happening.

22:39.524 --> 22:40.609
So listen carefully.

22:40.692 --> 22:43.612
I never listen to anyone.
I only listen to my grandmother.

22:43.695 --> 22:45.447
Then consider me
your grandmother of the lamp.

22:45.530 --> 22:48.075
Just by being here, I'm going against her.
So screw off!

22:48.158 --> 22:50.535
That's the opposite of what you just said.

22:51.119 --> 22:53.205
983 years ago, remember?

22:54.164 --> 22:55.540
Do you not remember at all?

22:56.249 --> 22:57.250
You forgot already?

22:57.334 --> 23:00.003
Well, 983 years ago…

23:00.754 --> 23:02.422
Goryeo dynasty?

23:02.506 --> 23:04.633
Choi Soo-jong was playing
the army general,

23:04.716 --> 23:07.010
-was going on about some king or another…
-[groaning]

23:07.094 --> 23:09.221
…before the whole thing fell.
You realize I wasn't there!

23:09.304 --> 23:10.764
You sure we go that far back?

23:10.847 --> 23:13.600
Yes, we go that far back!
Look how long my hair has grown.

23:13.683 --> 23:16.520
[sighs] Wow. It takes time, you know.

23:16.603 --> 23:17.646
Sure.

23:17.729 --> 23:20.565
You're telling me,
during all that time, your hair grew,

23:21.233 --> 23:22.984
-but your beard didn't?
-[gasps]

23:25.695 --> 23:27.072
Of course…

23:28.573 --> 23:31.076
I can see why you ask that, but…

23:31.159 --> 23:34.454
Well, I'm very self-conscious
and I like to change the subject.

23:34.538 --> 23:35.580
So just cooperate.

23:35.664 --> 23:38.834
You know how bad it was
living in that lamp for 983 years?

23:38.917 --> 23:39.751
I'll cooperate.

23:41.002 --> 23:42.212
Just how bad was it?

23:43.255 --> 23:46.174
[sighs] It took away my dignity.
[chuckles dryly]

23:48.343 --> 23:51.429
Goryeo. Goryeo. Where's Goryeo?

23:51.513 --> 23:54.724
Once I get out,
I'll obliterate it! [pants]

23:54.808 --> 23:57.686
[animal growling] The thing is, Master,
the land called "Goryeo"

23:57.769 --> 24:04.192
no longer exists as it was overthrown
by someone called "Yi Seong-gye."

24:04.276 --> 24:07.487
They also believe
in the cycle of death and rebirth.

24:07.571 --> 24:10.740
Something "carnage," was it?

24:11.908 --> 24:13.285
Reincarnation.

24:14.119 --> 24:15.537
[chuckles softly]

24:15.620 --> 24:17.122
There is reincarnation.

24:17.956 --> 24:19.040
[sighs]

24:19.124 --> 24:21.251
Sade, you need to go
to that country this instant.

24:22.252 --> 24:23.587
Search it.

24:23.670 --> 24:26.006
Don't stop until
you've scoured every corner.

24:27.924 --> 24:30.135
See if that girl lives again.

24:32.721 --> 24:35.432
-[growling]
-[suspenseful music plays]

24:50.155 --> 24:51.948
Oh. Excuse me. Uh…

24:53.742 --> 24:54.993
[sighs]

24:55.076 --> 24:56.828
-Oh, excuse me.
-[man grunts softly]

24:59.080 --> 25:00.790
Oh. Oh. Ah.

25:00.874 --> 25:03.043
-Uh, have you…
-Hmm?

25:03.793 --> 25:05.003
Have you seen a woman like this?

25:05.629 --> 25:09.257
[man 2] I'm not sure. I don't think
I've seen her around these parts.

25:12.302 --> 25:13.720
[pillar crumbling]

25:18.642 --> 25:20.727
[grunting]

25:20.810 --> 25:22.437
[screaming]

25:22.520 --> 25:26.066
[Iblis] Even after 600 years had passed,
I upheld my dignity.

25:26.775 --> 25:27.609
Though…

25:27.692 --> 25:28.526
F U

25:28.610 --> 25:30.278
…the lamp took a bit of a beating.

25:30.362 --> 25:31.529
-[grunts]
-[rumbling]

25:31.613 --> 25:32.656
[panting]

25:34.532 --> 25:35.617
[sighs]

25:35.700 --> 25:37.661
Being here is getting old.

25:38.286 --> 25:41.748
Why do I only get one piece of furniture?
I can't even lie down on it.

25:42.958 --> 25:44.334
I know you're listening!

25:46.044 --> 25:47.254
Hello?

25:47.337 --> 25:48.296
F U

25:48.380 --> 25:49.381
Huh?

25:50.173 --> 25:51.883
F U

25:55.136 --> 25:56.805
[breathes heavily]

25:58.265 --> 25:59.099
That girl.

26:00.767 --> 26:02.811
I'm coming for you, lump of clay!

26:03.687 --> 26:07.774
[Sade] Something called an automobile
has been invented, Master!

26:07.857 --> 26:11.403
They're big things with wheels
that roll around on their own.

26:11.486 --> 26:15.115
I'm telling you so you're not alarmed
or act too old-fashioned when you're out.

26:15.198 --> 26:16.866
[Iblis] Sade would come by
from time to time

26:16.950 --> 26:18.743
to let me know how the world had changed.

26:18.827 --> 26:21.579
Oh, also, when I visited the East,

26:21.663 --> 26:24.541
I took on a new local body and face,

26:24.624 --> 26:27.043
and it's my favorite one.

26:27.127 --> 26:28.753
It's got perks, like,

26:28.837 --> 26:32.882
my lady of the household
keeps giving me food.

26:34.217 --> 26:36.970
Then, at year 800,

26:37.679 --> 26:40.098
I was becoming frustrated, you know.

26:41.182 --> 26:43.101
I had sent so many humans to hell.

26:43.184 --> 26:47.230
And out of all those humans,
only one had a pure soul.

26:47.314 --> 26:48.898
So why was I getting the blame?

26:49.441 --> 26:50.942
Am I right? Huh?

26:51.901 --> 26:55.989
It's strange.
I was actually missing you so much.

26:56.072 --> 26:59.117
I yearned for your reincarnation, hoping…

27:00.577 --> 27:03.496
that you yearned to meet
a spirit like me as well.

27:03.580 --> 27:06.291
I dreamt of so many ways to ruin you

27:06.374 --> 27:08.960
and so many ways to cause you pain.

27:09.044 --> 27:10.462
And then,

27:10.545 --> 27:12.630
when the 900th year grew near, I prayed.

27:13.423 --> 27:14.507
I called out.

27:15.216 --> 27:17.844
Please give me one more…

27:17.927 --> 27:19.304
[snoring]

27:21.681 --> 27:22.515
Hey.

27:23.808 --> 27:27.062
You're sleeping before a genie?
Wait, when did you stop listening?

27:27.145 --> 27:29.147
Did you make it to the 600th year?

27:30.482 --> 27:32.108
Do I have to start over?

27:33.818 --> 27:34.736
Seriously?

27:35.779 --> 27:36.780
[sighs]

27:38.656 --> 27:40.033
[rattling]

27:58.718 --> 28:00.512
What the hell does that say?

28:01.346 --> 28:03.640
[Iblis] It says you shouldn't shake it,

28:03.723 --> 28:05.975
or an ill-tempered genie might get angry.

28:07.310 --> 28:08.353
[chuckles]

28:08.436 --> 28:11.189
But you were actually decent at first.
Even alluring.

28:11.272 --> 28:13.316
I really appreciate that.

28:13.942 --> 28:16.611
-So you were listening.
-Only because it finally got interesting.

28:16.694 --> 28:17.654
Hmm?

28:20.156 --> 28:21.950
I mean, less boring in general.

28:23.451 --> 28:26.287
So after you prayed, then what?
He responded?

28:26.371 --> 28:27.247
[huffs]

28:28.123 --> 28:28.957
Oh, yes.

28:31.876 --> 28:33.670
[fireworks crackling and booming]

28:33.753 --> 28:36.214
[upbeat music playing]

28:37.507 --> 28:39.467
[God] Dear Iblis,

28:40.635 --> 28:43.096
I shall fulfill your requests.

28:45.682 --> 28:51.396
Yet, should the day come
when you prostrate to my creations again,

28:53.064 --> 28:56.276
you will be beheaded.

28:58.361 --> 28:59.404
What did you pray for?

29:00.196 --> 29:01.656
"Please, give me one more."

29:01.740 --> 29:02.782
"One more…"

29:02.866 --> 29:03.783
[sighs]

29:04.576 --> 29:05.910
Chance.

29:08.037 --> 29:09.038
Please…

29:11.124 --> 29:14.002
I beg you. One more chance.

29:15.003 --> 29:17.422
If a creation of yours summons me

29:18.256 --> 29:20.133
and becomes my new master,

29:21.426 --> 29:24.179
if they are a truly righteous human,

29:24.262 --> 29:27.015
I will banish myself to hell forevermore.

29:29.142 --> 29:29.976
[sighs]

29:30.059 --> 29:33.229
But if I am able to corrupt them…

29:38.026 --> 29:39.944
then I will be freed!

29:40.028 --> 29:44.157
I ask you, then, grant me the freedom
to move as I wish between heaven and hell.

29:45.825 --> 29:48.369
Sure. Things wouldn't be that different,

29:48.453 --> 29:50.705
but it's in the details. Yeah?

29:51.498 --> 29:52.999
Yeah?

29:55.084 --> 29:56.252
-[sighs]
-[rumbling]

29:56.336 --> 29:59.172
-[grunting and groaning]
-[comical music plays]

30:04.219 --> 30:05.386
And at long last…

30:06.012 --> 30:06.846
[gasps]

30:06.930 --> 30:08.556
…a new master appeared.

30:08.640 --> 30:09.474
[gasps]

30:11.643 --> 30:14.062
But after all that, it's you again?

30:14.938 --> 30:16.731
-[smooth jazz plays]
-I thought it'd be good.

30:16.815 --> 30:18.733
But you haven't exactly been playing fair.

30:18.817 --> 30:19.859
Not fair how?

30:19.943 --> 30:22.278
Well, you clearly do not fear
or respect me.

30:22.362 --> 30:24.781
But you are just a human.

30:24.864 --> 30:26.616
This time, I shall prove him wrong.

30:26.699 --> 30:28.701
I'll show how corruptible humans are.

30:28.785 --> 30:31.621
How terrible his creation really is.

30:31.704 --> 30:32.539
Ha!

30:33.248 --> 30:34.249
Huh?

30:34.332 --> 30:36.292
Why are you bothering me
with all this nonsense?

30:36.376 --> 30:38.044
-I'm eating.
-Hmm?

30:40.088 --> 30:42.507
-Hmm?
-So, what do you want from me?

30:42.590 --> 30:43.508
Oh.

30:44.801 --> 30:46.719
Have we not discussed that yet?

30:48.054 --> 30:50.139
Oh, that's right.

30:50.223 --> 30:53.184
I want all your wishes.

30:53.268 --> 30:55.520
Not one, not two, but all three.

30:56.187 --> 30:57.063
Few ground rules.

30:58.147 --> 30:59.482
No bringing back the dead.

31:00.149 --> 31:01.860
No traveling to the future.

31:02.944 --> 31:04.404
Otherwise, anything you want,

31:05.113 --> 31:06.739
your wish…

31:08.199 --> 31:09.450
is my command.

31:09.534 --> 31:10.451
[ting]

31:10.535 --> 31:12.495
[seagulls squawking]

31:13.121 --> 31:13.955
[chuckles]

31:15.123 --> 31:16.833
Your look is alluring…

31:17.458 --> 31:18.293
to tempt me.

31:18.918 --> 31:22.463
That's right. Any sin you desire.

31:22.547 --> 31:23.965
You're evil.

31:24.048 --> 31:26.259
Huh? It's that obvious?

31:28.177 --> 31:29.679
You're right, I suppose.

31:30.471 --> 31:32.891
-I've been evil since before Christ.
-We're done.

31:33.433 --> 31:35.435
Or my first wish will be for you to die.

31:35.518 --> 31:36.978
Hey, hey. [laughs]

31:37.061 --> 31:39.439
It's strange that you were born like this.

31:39.522 --> 31:42.400
Was that version of you
all those years ago just pulling my leg?

31:42.483 --> 31:45.111
Or were you not actually virtuous,
just inarticulate?

31:48.781 --> 31:49.782
I was virtuous?

31:51.993 --> 31:53.244
Me?

31:53.328 --> 31:58.374
Master! The girl was finally reincarnated!

31:58.458 --> 32:04.797
But a war broke out and she died valiantly
fighting alongside a certain admiral!

32:05.673 --> 32:08.635
Well, it was Yi Sun-sin!

32:08.718 --> 32:11.930
I have located the girl once more!

32:12.013 --> 32:13.973
But she has already died!

32:14.057 --> 32:17.143
This time, she was helping
another soul again.

32:17.226 --> 32:20.146
Ah, it was Ahn Jung-geun!

32:21.147 --> 32:23.274
You were selfless and noble
for three of your lives,

32:23.358 --> 32:25.068
but I guess this one is different.

32:25.151 --> 32:27.278
Given how much
you like brandishing knifes.

32:27.362 --> 32:29.781
[grunts] It's actually great.

32:29.864 --> 32:32.909
Yes, let's corrupt you properly this time.

32:32.992 --> 32:36.287
Now, at its core,
corruption requires pleasure. Hmm.

32:36.371 --> 32:41.209
Master, I shall bestow
the greatest pleasures upon you today.

32:41.292 --> 32:43.086
-Bring me a camel!
-[gong rings]

32:43.795 --> 32:44.879
I've called an Uber.

32:46.422 --> 32:48.591
Hmm? What is an "Uber"?

32:48.675 --> 32:50.802
We don't ride camels now, only Ubers.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.846
Right. And an Uber is?

32:53.930 --> 32:55.848
[amusing music plays]

32:55.932 --> 32:57.266
And why should I tell you?

32:57.350 --> 32:59.519
Stop talking in circles.

33:00.228 --> 33:01.312
[Iblis groans]

33:01.938 --> 33:04.357
Actually… [chuckles]

33:04.440 --> 33:06.693
I admire your propensity for rudeness.

33:06.776 --> 33:09.821
Uber? Right,
it's been almost a millennium.

33:09.904 --> 33:11.572
The world has surely evolved quite a bit.

33:11.656 --> 33:15.076
So it's obvious
that I would be a smitch confused.

33:15.159 --> 33:16.661
I shall remain calm.

33:16.744 --> 33:18.162
[breathes deeply]

33:18.246 --> 33:20.748
[engine roaring]

33:20.832 --> 33:21.958
[shrieks]

33:22.041 --> 33:23.876
Damn that Sade!

33:23.960 --> 33:27.755
My servant didn't say there were
two-wheeled things as well as four!

33:28.506 --> 33:30.383
-[sighs]
-Whoopsie.

33:30.466 --> 33:31.342
Huh?

33:33.678 --> 33:34.887
[gasps]

33:39.559 --> 33:42.061
-Uh--
-[tool whirring]

33:42.145 --> 33:43.187
[whirring over cell phone]

33:43.271 --> 33:44.814
[shrieks, gasps]

33:44.897 --> 33:47.316
-[whirring over cell phone]
-What is that?

33:48.359 --> 33:49.861
It's making an evil sound.

33:50.486 --> 33:52.071
-Ugh.
-[whirring over cell phone]

33:52.155 --> 33:52.989
[gasps]

33:53.072 --> 33:53.906
[whirring stops]

33:54.949 --> 33:56.117
Grandma, I'm fine.

33:56.826 --> 33:59.495
Right now? Just sightseeing.

34:00.121 --> 34:01.622
[grandma] All right. Good.

34:01.706 --> 34:03.499
You're taking your medication?

34:04.584 --> 34:05.877
All right, all right.

34:05.960 --> 34:08.087
ADMISSION TO NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY

34:08.171 --> 34:09.297
Don't eat too many cold foods.

34:09.380 --> 34:12.050
And watch out for any men
who speak out of line.

34:12.133 --> 34:14.761
And forget any men who call you beautiful.

34:14.844 --> 34:18.723
If any men won't let you in peace,
you just let me handle it. All right?

34:18.806 --> 34:20.224
[Ka-young] She says to put you on.

34:20.308 --> 34:21.976
[Iblis] Put what on? A new face?

34:22.060 --> 34:24.562
But this face is designed
to be attracted to anyone

34:24.645 --> 34:26.856
-for the next thousand years.
-I'm-- I'm not understanding.

34:26.939 --> 34:28.608
Was that a man with her?

34:29.609 --> 34:30.985
Who's speaking?

34:31.069 --> 34:33.279
Ka-young? Hel-- [blows]

34:34.197 --> 34:35.615
Um, hello?

34:35.698 --> 34:38.618
[Ka-young] The reason I haven't killed
anyone was because of my grandma's rule.

34:41.120 --> 34:43.456
I dealt with the urge in other ways.
Nothing beats fatigue.

34:43.539 --> 34:44.373
[man] Uh, beating?

34:45.374 --> 34:46.292
Oh, wait. Oh… [chuckles]

34:48.961 --> 34:51.547
-Nothing beats fatigue. Got it. [laughs]
-[Ka-young] Yeah.

34:51.631 --> 34:54.634
Every day from when I was eight
until I went to college, my grandma and I

34:54.717 --> 34:57.553
would plant sesame, harvest sesame,
plant chilies, harvest chilies.

34:57.637 --> 34:58.679
A FAMILY-ORIENTED PSYCHOPATH

34:58.763 --> 34:59.764
[grunts]

35:00.807 --> 35:03.893
[sighs] I was so spent.
I also had to study and excel in school.

35:06.395 --> 35:09.148
I was so exploited for labor
that I just wanted to…

35:09.732 --> 35:11.859
-[ominous music plays]
-…murder something.

35:12.860 --> 35:15.363
-And, well, then it'd be morning.
-[man] Oh. Oh. [chuckles]

35:15.446 --> 35:17.281
HIGH-FUNCTIONING PSYCHOPATH
SETTING A GOOD EXAMPLE

35:17.365 --> 35:18.908
Mm. Hmm. Huh. I see.

35:18.991 --> 35:21.953
Ooh, I'm getting chills. [chuckles]
You're so funny, ma'am.

35:22.036 --> 35:22.912
NO, IT'S NOT FUNNY

35:22.995 --> 35:24.330
-Don't call me that.
-Uh-huh.

35:24.413 --> 35:25.540
THEN WHAT'S WITH THE ATTITUDE?

35:25.623 --> 35:28.084
-So you're a country guy now?
-Yes.

35:28.918 --> 35:29.752
-Got a car?
-Yes…

35:31.546 --> 35:34.298
If you need service on it,
I give new customers discounts.

35:36.259 --> 35:38.052
[chuckles] Ma'am--
Oh, no. Uh, Ka-young?

35:38.136 --> 35:42.098
Um, you're just so scary
and still funny. [chuckling]

35:42.181 --> 35:45.309
By the way, I'm just so curious.

35:45.393 --> 35:48.437
Do psychopaths
really not know what love is?

35:48.521 --> 35:51.232
Like, being willing to sacrifice yourself
for another? [chuckles]

35:51.315 --> 35:52.608
I think I could kill…

35:53.734 --> 35:55.069
for another person.

35:56.195 --> 35:57.655
Does that count as love?

35:57.738 --> 35:59.448
[laughing]

36:01.701 --> 36:02.618
Wow.

36:02.702 --> 36:03.536
[hits key]

36:03.619 --> 36:05.079
[chuckles]

36:05.163 --> 36:06.998
VIDEO UPLOADING

36:07.081 --> 36:09.417
[traditional music playing]

36:11.169 --> 36:13.087
[girl] Oh, wow. My goodness!

36:13.171 --> 36:15.840
Mom, I wanna buy everything here.

36:15.923 --> 36:16.924
[woman] Right?

36:17.008 --> 36:18.885
[Ka-young] Oh, wow. My goodness.

36:18.968 --> 36:21.596
Tour guide, I want to buy
everything here. Oh!

36:21.679 --> 36:24.307
[guide] Oh? What?
Why are you telling me that?

36:24.390 --> 36:26.350
Do it. Your three wishes.

36:26.434 --> 36:28.269
Make them immediately. Do it right now.

36:28.352 --> 36:30.104
[Ka-young] Get lost.
Find yourself a barber.

36:30.188 --> 36:31.147
Do you wish it?

36:31.856 --> 36:33.816
Want to get sliced in half again?

36:37.528 --> 36:40.531
[hesitates] Why would you say that?
What does that mean?

36:41.824 --> 36:42.742
[mutters]

36:48.039 --> 36:50.041
Those lamps. Oh, my goodness!

36:50.666 --> 36:51.626
[chuckles]

36:52.210 --> 36:54.045
-Oh, my goodness-uh.
-[cell phone vibrates]

36:57.673 --> 36:58.507
CHOI MIN-JI

36:58.591 --> 37:01.928
[Min-ji] You know gifts after a trip
overseas are mandatory, right?

37:02.845 --> 37:04.597
What do most people buy in Dubai?

37:05.598 --> 37:07.767
-Well, Chanel, of course. [chuckles]
-Right.

37:08.517 --> 37:09.685
I'll buy them that.

37:10.519 --> 37:12.230
I suppose there's a mall around?

37:13.564 --> 37:16.692
Ah. I was just making a joke.

37:18.027 --> 37:20.905
I was also making a joke. Heh.

37:22.490 --> 37:25.409
Ah. You were, weren't you? [laughing]

37:26.035 --> 37:27.954
That was very funny. [chuckles]

37:28.037 --> 37:30.331
No, the souvenirs are here, these lamps.

37:30.414 --> 37:34.085
Goodness. Do you think
that a genie will show up if I rub it?

37:34.168 --> 37:36.045
Do it. Your three wishes.

37:36.128 --> 37:38.256
Make them all. Do it immediately.

37:38.339 --> 37:40.132
I told you to get lost.

37:40.216 --> 37:43.928
You chose the wrong person.
I have rules and routines.

37:44.011 --> 37:45.221
They keep my life going.

37:46.055 --> 37:48.975
So I don't need things like silly wishes.

37:49.892 --> 37:51.143
Excuse me.

37:52.270 --> 37:54.146
Who is it you're talking to?

37:56.607 --> 37:57.733
The Genie.

37:57.817 --> 37:59.986
This bastard hasn't shut up
since yesterday.

38:05.157 --> 38:06.909
[amusing music plays]

38:06.993 --> 38:07.827
[tourists gasp]

38:07.910 --> 38:10.288
[girl] What in the world?
She's so strange.

38:12.498 --> 38:17.044
Oh. I'm only visible to you.
One of my magical quirks.

38:18.462 --> 38:19.630
Oh, you asshole.

38:19.714 --> 38:21.882
You son of a bitch
that can't even grow a beard.

38:21.966 --> 38:23.551
You and your stupidly long hair.

38:23.634 --> 38:26.512
Why can't you pester someone else?
I told you to piss off!

38:26.595 --> 38:29.307
Why the fuck can't anyone else see you?
I look crazy!

38:30.016 --> 38:32.476
Well, you're corrupt already.

38:33.728 --> 38:35.021
Amazingly corrupt.

38:35.104 --> 38:36.939
All right. That means we're almost there.

38:37.023 --> 38:38.190
Hmm?

38:40.192 --> 38:41.193
[Ka-young sighs]

38:43.321 --> 38:44.572
[engine revs]

38:47.450 --> 38:48.451
[screams]

38:51.954 --> 38:53.164
[water trickling]

38:54.623 --> 38:55.833
[door shuts]

38:55.916 --> 38:57.251
Hi. How are you?

38:57.335 --> 38:58.753
Ooh, that's salty.

39:00.755 --> 39:01.630
Wow.

39:02.340 --> 39:03.257
[chuckles]

39:08.387 --> 39:09.347
[sighs]

39:09.972 --> 39:11.265
[seething breath]

39:11.849 --> 39:15.102
One dirham. One dirham.

39:16.187 --> 39:17.271
One dirham.

39:17.980 --> 39:18.981
One dirham.

39:20.232 --> 39:21.359
One dirham.

39:22.276 --> 39:25.112
-[man] One dirham? Just one?
-Yes. One dirham.

39:25.196 --> 39:26.697
One dirham. Yeah.

39:27.406 --> 39:28.449
[coins clacking]

39:31.243 --> 39:32.078
[clink]

39:33.704 --> 39:34.872
[coin clinks]

39:34.955 --> 39:36.082
[sighs]

39:36.165 --> 39:37.083
[coin clinks]

39:37.917 --> 39:39.418
This is insanity.

39:39.502 --> 39:41.128
Just try and throw me out again.

39:42.046 --> 39:44.840
I can't leave your side.
We're tied together.

39:44.924 --> 39:46.133
[coin clinks]

39:49.095 --> 39:50.513
Maybe I could swap you out.

39:52.181 --> 39:54.433
-Are you the only genie?
-No.

39:54.517 --> 39:56.602
But I'm the most famous genie.

39:56.685 --> 39:58.813
[chuckles softly]
What do you have planned?

40:07.196 --> 40:08.948
[rattling]

40:20.292 --> 40:21.293
[gasps]

40:24.296 --> 40:26.298
[distorted gong rings]

40:28.551 --> 40:30.302
[amusing music plays]

40:30.386 --> 40:32.972
What? Do all genies look the same?

40:35.850 --> 40:38.310
Are you familiar
with a genie with long hair?

40:38.394 --> 40:39.603
Yes, I am.

40:40.438 --> 40:43.566
I can just tell you're looking for a way
to defeat or eliminate him.

40:43.649 --> 40:46.777
And you are perhaps
thinking of fighting magic with magic?

40:46.861 --> 40:50.406
[chuckles] I've never thought of that.
A very refreshing approach.

40:50.489 --> 40:54.493
But this spirit, he's the only genie
in this world who grants wishes.

40:56.662 --> 40:58.372
If you've seen him, you'd know.

40:58.456 --> 41:01.876
There's no space he can't inhabit,
and he's perfect from head to toe.

41:01.959 --> 41:03.836
The walking epitome of dignity.

41:03.919 --> 41:06.380
Weaknesses? Drawbacks? What even are they?

41:06.464 --> 41:07.965
But getting rid of him is easy.

41:08.048 --> 41:08.883
He will leave

41:09.758 --> 41:11.969
once your wishes
have been made. [chuckles]

41:12.052 --> 41:13.721
-On your left.
-Hmm?

41:13.804 --> 41:15.347
-[sharp thud]
-[grunts softly]

41:16.098 --> 41:17.391
Stop tricking me.

41:17.475 --> 41:19.810
[chuckles] That was pretty painful.

41:19.894 --> 41:22.396
You've been anything but fair
and righteous and dignified yourself.

41:22.480 --> 41:23.939
You rubbed every lamp you could find.

41:24.023 --> 41:26.358
That's from The Art of War. Fantastic.

41:26.442 --> 41:27.276
Hmm.

41:29.236 --> 41:32.156
If you lose the upper hand,
just change the subject.

41:33.532 --> 41:35.618
You pinned your hair. It's pretty.

41:35.701 --> 41:36.744
[smacks lips]

41:36.827 --> 41:39.038
I have far too much of it to carry around.

41:39.121 --> 41:40.706
But it's obvious that you're lying.

41:41.373 --> 41:44.919
If the conversation gets awkward,
just make it even more awkward.

41:46.504 --> 41:50.132
A distraction from your sad facial hair.
How is it you know my language?

41:50.216 --> 41:51.175
Hmm?

41:52.510 --> 41:53.844
[smacks lips]

41:53.928 --> 41:57.806
Oh, I'm not speaking in your language,
I'm speaking in Arabic.

41:57.890 --> 41:59.225
Being a Genie means

41:59.308 --> 42:02.269
it always sounds like
I'm speaking the local tongue.

42:02.353 --> 42:04.563
-So speak in Arabic.
-What?

42:04.647 --> 42:06.941
Well, you're not Arabic. It's impossible.

42:07.024 --> 42:09.026
Well, I'm not a person either.

42:10.528 --> 42:12.905
[in Arabic] How much is this?
Where is the toilet?

42:12.988 --> 42:15.282
No cilantro, please.

42:15.366 --> 42:17.034
-[in English] Good?
-Terrible Arabic.

42:17.117 --> 42:18.202
Native speaker.

42:18.285 --> 42:20.371
Who would benefit from beginner lessons.

42:20.454 --> 42:21.497
That's subjective.

42:21.580 --> 42:23.332
Have you always been so aggressive?

42:23.415 --> 42:25.292
If so, that's pretty good news.

42:25.376 --> 42:27.878
Grandma healthy?
Not one single wish to make?

42:27.962 --> 42:28.879
Do you remember nothing?

42:29.880 --> 42:32.341
-I see you give as well as you take.
-Hmm.

42:32.424 --> 42:34.134
Enough. Can you fly?

42:34.802 --> 42:36.804
Movies with spirits, vampires,

42:36.887 --> 42:38.847
they all just fly off, all the way…

42:38.931 --> 42:39.974
[grunts]

42:40.057 --> 42:41.058
[chuckles]

42:41.141 --> 42:42.101
[gasps]

42:43.769 --> 42:46.855
[dramatic rock fusion music]

43:15.217 --> 43:16.427
[whooshing]

43:24.518 --> 43:26.145
[vehicles honking]

43:26.895 --> 43:30.274
[man in Arabic] Move out of the way,
crazy! Are you trying to get killed?

43:30.357 --> 43:32.234
[in English] He's saying he likes us.

43:33.110 --> 43:35.863
[dramatic rock music continues playing]

44:04.558 --> 44:05.559
[Iblis] "Can I fly?"

44:06.602 --> 44:09.605
Did that answer it?
What was it you said? Vampire?

44:11.940 --> 44:12.900
Wow.

44:13.776 --> 44:14.610
Wow.

44:16.820 --> 44:18.822
-Wow.
-[chuckles]

44:19.573 --> 44:21.408
You really are a genie.

44:22.951 --> 44:24.912
Allow me to scream now from sheer joy.

44:25.788 --> 44:27.915
[chuckles]
I'm familiar with that reaction.

44:28.791 --> 44:29.833
Okay!

44:36.799 --> 44:38.300
[screams]

44:39.885 --> 44:41.470
[screams]

44:42.721 --> 44:44.473
[screams]

44:54.566 --> 44:56.360
Wait, what's that look?

44:58.278 --> 45:00.114
I've never seen that expression.

45:01.156 --> 45:02.491
This is real happiness.

45:03.575 --> 45:04.618
Happiness?

45:05.244 --> 45:06.286
Hmm…

45:06.370 --> 45:08.831
-Does that mean you have a wish?
-No.

45:10.624 --> 45:12.042
I finally have a chance.

45:12.835 --> 45:14.336
The perfect location.

45:15.629 --> 45:17.214
The perfect target.

45:18.048 --> 45:19.258
[Iblis gasps]

45:20.050 --> 45:22.761
If you fall this high up,
which bone would crack first?

45:23.387 --> 45:24.388
Hmm?

45:25.013 --> 45:26.432
Don't tell my grandma, okay?

45:27.015 --> 45:27.850
Huh?

45:32.479 --> 45:35.816
[screaming]

45:35.899 --> 45:42.072
[shouting] Who even is your grandmother?

45:42.614 --> 45:43.615
[splat]

45:44.324 --> 45:46.493
Hmm? That was pretty quick.

45:46.577 --> 45:48.579
[disquieting music fading in]

45:54.501 --> 45:56.837
Unexpected. You startled me.

45:56.920 --> 45:58.255
You startled me.

45:59.715 --> 46:02.092
Most would be alarmed
after they've killed someone,

46:02.176 --> 46:03.510
but you're only just alarmed now.

46:03.594 --> 46:05.762
[bones shuffling]

46:05.846 --> 46:08.724
I should have slowed down.
Don't you think?

46:10.601 --> 46:12.394
Your arm broke first? Not your skull?

46:14.646 --> 46:16.273
Depends on the rotations.

46:17.274 --> 46:20.319
Also if it's a straight drop
or if you hit the side of the building.

46:21.153 --> 46:23.864
I hit the building,
so I flew back a little sooner.

46:24.615 --> 46:28.285
My skull was indeed broken,
but I repaired myself on my way back up.

46:28.368 --> 46:29.536
Uh-huh?

46:33.415 --> 46:34.541
I know that look.

46:37.544 --> 46:38.504
Real…

46:39.796 --> 46:40.797
rage.

46:41.381 --> 46:42.382
[chuckles softly]

46:43.050 --> 46:44.176
If you know this look,

46:44.259 --> 46:47.054
then you shouldn't have done that, Master.

46:48.055 --> 46:50.390
-[gagging]
-[somber music plays]

46:52.601 --> 46:54.353
[choking]

47:01.652 --> 47:05.155
I accept… punishment.

47:05.239 --> 47:06.615
So…

47:07.366 --> 47:10.410
make sure we are punished right.

47:11.036 --> 47:12.538
You and me.

47:14.540 --> 47:15.624
[gags]

47:15.707 --> 47:17.084
I hoped you'd be different.

47:18.001 --> 47:19.920
Never thought you'd be this different.

47:20.003 --> 47:21.463
[choking]

47:21.547 --> 47:22.548
What even are you?

47:24.591 --> 47:25.592
Beg.

47:26.176 --> 47:27.177
Ask for your life.

47:27.261 --> 47:28.845
[choking]

47:28.929 --> 47:30.806
Tell me it's your first wish.

47:32.266 --> 47:34.268
-Make it.
-[grunts]

47:34.351 --> 47:35.894
None of my wishes

47:36.979 --> 47:39.773
won't benefit in any way, I see that now.

47:39.856 --> 47:41.024
[chuckles lightly]

47:42.109 --> 47:43.110
Clever.

47:43.986 --> 47:44.820
That's right.

47:44.903 --> 47:48.198
Once your three wishes are made
and I am no longer imprisoned,

47:48.282 --> 47:49.700
I will destroy you.

47:50.325 --> 47:51.451
[grunts]

47:51.535 --> 47:52.578
[chuckles]

47:52.661 --> 47:54.288
[inhales sharply, grunts]

47:54.371 --> 47:55.414
If that's your plan,

47:56.164 --> 47:57.791
then forget the wishes.

47:58.458 --> 48:00.502
Just throw me off right now.

48:02.629 --> 48:05.382
I'm… [laughing]

48:05.465 --> 48:08.385
having such fun! [cackling]

48:09.761 --> 48:11.930
[continues cackling]

48:19.521 --> 48:21.523
[continues cackling]

48:22.733 --> 48:25.569
[dramatic rock fusion music]
